 "_about": [
  "Source tiers for theses/bin/news_pack.py. A headline is only a lead: the tier says how far to trust that the story exists as written, never that it is true.",
  "Rule, in order. (1) The RSS source field, compared case-insensitively and ignoring a leading 'www.', is looked up in each tier's 'names'. (2) If the source field is a domain (it contains a dot and no space), or the link is not a Google News redirect, that domain is compared with each tier's 'domains': it matches a listed domain exactly or as a subdomain (finance.yahoo.com matches yahoo.com). Tier 1 is tried first, then tier 2, then tier 3. (3) A source that matches nothing is tier 3. (4) A tier 2 headline whose title matches any 'tier3_title_patterns' entry is moved to tier 3: that is how a Zacks, Simply Wall St, StockStory or Insider Monkey item syndicated under a Yahoo Finance or MSN byline is told apart from original reporting. Tier 1 is never demoted.",
  "Every per-ticker link in docs/news is a news.google.com redirect, so in practice the source field decides. Edit the lists here, not in the code, and commit the change: the pack records which rule placed each headline."
 ],
